# C106 -- sulukFmt.branch/race/quorum: first-class branching, join policies, aggregation, graph I/O. Extends
# C104/C105 same-day. Operator quoted C105's own ADR text back verbatim ("It still is not a general conditional
# workflow engine... you still do not have arbitrary branching, rich match/switch semantics, or a fully general
# control-flow language") and asked for four concrete additions: a first-class branch mechanism, a first-class join
# policy, a first-class aggregation/result-mapping mechanism, graph-level input/output schemas -- supplying a
# concrete type sketch as a starting point. Given the concurrency-correctness stakes of hand-building join-policy
# primitives Effect has no built-in for, a design was drafted, then INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED (Effect API grounding)
# and CRITICALLY REVIEWED (concurrency correctness + API consistency, two parallel reviewers) BEFORE a line of
# production code was written. ADR C106. @>=0.85
claim c106_verified_and_reviewed_before_implementation: Bool @>=0.85 = True
falsified_when c106_verified_and_reviewed_before_implementation == False

# A REAL, HANG-CAUSING BUG WAS FOUND DURING DESIGN, BEFORE ANY PRODUCTION CODE EXISTED. Effect has no single
# built-in combinator for either join policy needed: Effect.raceAll races on FIRST SETTLEMENT (a branch that merely
# FAILS fast still "wins" over one that later succeeds -- wrong for "any"); Effect.firstSuccessOf runs its
# candidates SEQUENTIALLY, not concurrently. Both had to be hand-built (raceForSuccess/raceForQuorum, via Deferred +
# Effect.fork + Fiber.interruptAll). A first draft used Effect.matchEffect to observe each branch's outcome -- the
# verification pass found this only ever sees the plain Fail/E channel, silently dropping Die (a defect) and
# Interrupt: if the LAST branch needed to settle a race died instead of failing cleanly, the accounting counter
# would never reach zero and the whole race would hang FOREVER, leaking the awaiting fiber. Fixed with Effect.exit
# (converts EVERY outcome -- Fail/Die/Interrupt -- into an inspectable Exit), verified against the real effect
# package source before being written, locked in by a dedicated regression test (a branch that throws rather than
# Effect.fail's). A SECOND review pass then found three further hangs in the first corrected draft (effects=[],
# quorum<=0, quorum>effects.length) -- each fixed with an eager guard BEFORE forking anything. @>=0.9
claim c106_matchEffect_hang_bug_found_and_fixed_before_shipping: Bool @>=0.9 = True
falsified_when c106_matchEffect_hang_bug_found_and_fixed_before_shipping == False

# BUILT: sulukFmt.branch(cases, discriminator, opts?) -- real, type-checked conditional routing over a node's OWN
# declared cases (cases FIRST, so Cases resolves before discriminator is checked against it -- the reverse order
# was flagged as inference-hostile during review; the FINAL signature indexes Out/R/In off Cases[keyof Cases] via
# InOf/OutOf/ReqOf, mirroring sulukFmt.all's own already-working inference pattern, after an EARLIER signature using
# 3 independent generic params defeated TS's inference and required explicit type arguments in tests -- a real,
# caught-via-tsc bug in the FIRST implementation attempt, fixed before shipping). All cases share the same Out;
# errors/steps/store.invalidates UNION across cases; cost is the MAX across cases (not the sum sulukFmt/sulukFmt.all
# use) -- exactly one case executes per call, so summing would overstate the real, billed x-suluk-cost (a review
# finding, not part of the original sketch). opts.label adds a synthetic decision node whose shape is COMPUTED,
# never hand-set, as "branch"; the wire-level `when` on each branch edge is sourced structurally from
# Object.keys(cases), never free-form author prose. @>=0.85
claim c106_branch_type_checked_cases_first_max_cost: Bool @>=0.85 = True
falsified_when c106_branch_type_checked_cases_first_max_cost == False

# BUILT: sulukFmt.race(effects, opts?) / sulukFmt.quorum(effects, quorum, opts?) -- "any"/"quorum" JOIN POLICIES:
# fork every candidate concurrently; race resolves on first SUCCESS (interrupting the rest); quorum resolves once
# quorum-many succeed (an array, completion order; interrupting the rest); both fail eagerly once unreachable. Take
# a plain ARRAY not a keyed Record -- a review finding: TS does NOT actually enforce homogeneous Out across Record
# values the way the original sketch assumed, so Record bought a FALSE type-safety guarantee for these two unkeyed-
# result combinators (Record stays right for branch, which genuinely needs per-case keys). errors/cost UNION/SUM
# across all candidates (every one genuinely runs concurrently, unlike branch). opts.label adds a synthetic
# join:{policy}+aggregate:{strategy} node as the sole terminal. sulukFmt.all gains the SAME opts.label (unchanged
# default behavior -- still Effect.all, still object merge; labeling adds join:{policy:"all"}+
# aggregate:{strategy:"object"}, giving a labeled fan-out a defined resultNode where an unlabeled one still has
# none). @>=0.85
claim c106_race_quorum_array_based_all_gains_label: Bool @>=0.85 = True
falsified_when c106_race_quorum_array_based_all_gains_label == False

# BUILT: graph-level roots/input/output. roots mirrors terminals (recomputed at EVERY merge choke point, not just
# once -- a review finding: sequential edges retire the NEXT stage's root candidates the same way they retire
# prev's terminal candidates). input/output mirror resultNode's own honest reasoning exactly: present iff
# unambiguous (roots.length===1 / resultNode defined), taken from that single node's own input/output. output is
# explicitly documented as the pre-view-wrap domain shape (a review finding -- the original sketch didn't restate
# this at the graph level). A REQUIRED correctness fix from adding "branch" edges: isSuccessEdge was renamed
# isForwardEdge and extended to treat "branch" as forward-progress topology (like "success") -- only "error" edges
# are excluded from roots/terminals/resultNode computation; getting this wrong (treating branch like error) would
# have made every branch case and the decision node itself vanish from entry/terminal computation, a review-flagged
# blocking issue caught before it shipped. Node `shape` (renamed from the original sketch's `role`, which collided
# with the pre-existing ScenarioStep.role) is fully COMPUTED, never author-set. @>=0.85
claim c106_graph_io_roots_and_forward_edge_fix: Bool @>=0.85 = True
falsified_when c106_graph_io_roots_and_forward_edge_fix == False

# VERIFIED: @suluk/effect 115/115 tests pass (85 pre-existing from C104/C105 unchanged + 30 new), including REAL
# timing-sensitive concurrency tests: slow-success-beats-fast-failure, a losing branch actually gets INTERRUPTED
# (not left running in the background -- proven via Effect.onInterrupt), a DEFECT (thrown, not Effect.fail) on the
# last-standing candidate still surfaces correctly (the exact matchEffect bug this design was built around),
# quorum fails EAGERLY before a slow straggler would have resolved, quorum<=0 resolves [] without running anything,
# quorum>candidates dies rather than hanging, a race/quorum loser's OWN compensate does NOT fire when interrupted
# mid-flight (a deliberately tested boundary), branch/race/quorum cost aggregation (MAX vs SUM) is asserted, and
# lintRunGraph's cycle detection still catches a cycle formed by reusing a branch's own case node as a later
# pipeline stage. Full 30-package ecosystem sweep: ZERO typecheck errors. Every touched package's runtime suite
# green (effect 115, hono 81, core 66, drizzle 60, platform 149) -- zero regression. Same TWO pre-existing,
# unrelated failures as C104/C105 (admin's stale wrangler-deploy test; a drizzle-zod/nano-stores version-mismatch
# typecheck error in untouched files) -- confirmed unchanged, out of scope. @>=0.9
claim c106_verified_115_tests_zero_regression_full_sweep: Bool @>=0.9 = True
falsified_when c106_verified_115_tests_zero_regression_full_sweep == False

# DELIBERATELY STILL NOT BUILT, NAMED HONESTLY (not silently dropped): aggregate.strategy's "custom-keyed-merge"
# value from the original sketch (nothing produces it: all->"object", race->"first", quorum->"array" -- an
# unproduced enum value violates the facet's "absent unless meaningfully declared" discipline); a role:"fail" node
# classification (can't be computed purely from graph structure the way join/aggregate/branch can); a "portable"
# predicate/expression language, node-to-node symbolic value bindings (SulukRunValueRef/SulukRunBinding), a general
# error-routing model beyond a node's own declared cases, or a graph-level result-projection rule distinct from
# resultNode/output -- these are a CATEGORICALLY DIFFERENT, LARGER undertaking than anything in C104-C106: every
# combinator shipped here still routes through a REAL, type-checked TypeScript function the author writes; a
# JSON-encoded predicate/binding language would instead need a genuine INTERPRETER (evaluating predicate-shaped data
# against resolved runtime values), reopening exactly the drift risk this whole primitive has been built, three
# ADRs running, to avoid -- a decision requiring its own deliberate scoping pass, not a silent extension of this
# one. This ADR explicitly REVISES C093/C104/C105's "exactly two combinators" framing: sulukFmt (linear) and
# sulukFmt.all (unconditional fan-out) remain the base pair; branch/race/quorum are now real, additional
# combinators, each narrowly scoped the same way recover/compensate already are. @>=0.85
claim c106_deferred_items_and_revised_two_combinators_claim: Bool @>=0.85 = True
falsified_when c106_deferred_items_and_revised_two_combinators_claim == False
